From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:26:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 91/99] v8: e2k: make the LSX instructions of the layer of the
 qp operations of e2k-v5

WebAssembly SIMD on e2k: the 128-bit instructions of the backend (copied
from loong64) are LoongArch LSX.  la_asm.h now has the 222 of them that
V8 uses, made of the 128-bit (qp) operations of e2k-v5 (opcodes-qp.inc,
read back from GNU as by simd/gen_qp.py in the lab), with the semantics
measured on 8SV.  CpuFeatures::SupportsSimd128() is true.

- Loads and stores go through two ldd/std: ldqp/stqp want 16-byte
  alignment.
- No vector register is written by a 64-bit operation: a qp read soon
  after can see a stale high half.
- No literal operands in qp operations but where 64 bits are read: the
  high half of a literal is undefined.
- Unused LSX instructions are UNIMPLEMENTED().
